From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the window's surfaces lossless-compressed (fewer bytes per frame)

What: the IOSurface present makes its surfaces in Apple's lossless-
compressed forms through CoreVideo: 8-bit ones as '&BGA'
(kCVPixelFormatType_Lossless_32BGRA) instead of plain 'BGRA', half-float
ones (HDR, Extra brightness) as '&RhA'
(kCVPixelFormatType_Lossless_64RGBAHalf) instead of 'RGhA'; the layer
takes both half-float kinds for EDR. The GPU writes and reads them
compressed: QEMU's draw of each frame into the surface and WindowServer's
composite of the window move fewer bytes. Nothing may read these surfaces
back, on the CPU or with glReadPixels (it crashes on them): the boot logo's
readback reads the guest's texture, and the partial present's check mode
(OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_DAMAGE=check, omacvm-cocoa-present-damage.patch), which
reads the shown surface, keeps them plain. If one cannot
be made or bound to GL, surfaces of that kind (8-bit or half float) are
plain for the rest of the run (one warning in qemu.log); OMACVM_GL_LOSSLESS=0 keeps them plain. Shown as a layer's contents they
are checked on macOS 27 only (captured: an M1 Max at 120 Hz, an M2, an M4
on an external display; work/window-path/oncheck.m): older systems keep plain
surfaces. qemu.log says "cocoa: 8-bit surfaces lossless-compressed" (or
plain, or half-float) for the first surfaces and when it changes.

Why: what showing the VM's window costs is mostly moving its pixels, not
GPU time (taking WindowServer's colour matching out of its composite took
a third off its GPU time and nothing off the watts). MacBook Air M2, the
real VM full screen at 60 Hz, A/B/A/B: scrolling 4.45 W vs 4.65 W plain
(-0.20 W, -4 %), a 1080p30 video the same within the gauge's noise; the
same pixels (a 144-patch page: all identical) and frame rates. QEMU's own
draw: 20-25 % less GPU time. GL draws into these surfaces exactly (read
back through Core Image on an M1 Max, an M2 and an M4:
work/window-path/lbcheck.m).

Upstream: OmacVM only (QEMU's IOSurface present is OmacVM's).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-present-lossless.sh (the patched
ui/cocoa.m is wired as tested; the checks catch code without it).
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-extra-brightness.patch (before omacvm-cocoa-no-app-nap.patch).
diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
index 9a06add..77af768 100644
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -7407,6 +7407,27 @@ static void cocoa_gl_render(void)
 static uint32_t present_w, present_h;
 static bool present_deep;              /* half-float surfaces (10-bit scanout) */
 static bool present_linear;            /* half-float, extended linear sRGB: extra brightness */
+static bool present_packed;            /* the surfaces are lossless-compressed */
+static bool present_packed_half;       /* ... of half float (for the log) */
+static bool present_packed_logged;     /* the kind was logged once */
+
+/*
+ * OmacVM, lossless surfaces: the surfaces in Apple's lossless-compressed
+ * forms ('&BGA' for 8-bit, '&RhA' for half float: HDR and extra
+ * brightness; made through CoreVideo). The GPU writes and
+ * reads them compressed, so QEMU's draw into them and WindowServer's
+ * composite of the window move fewer bytes. Nothing may read them back: not
+ * on the CPU, not with glReadPixels (it crashes on them). The boot logo's
+ * readback reads the guest's texture; the partial present's check mode
+ * (OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_DAMAGE=check) reads the surfaces, so it keeps them
+ * plain. If one cannot be
+ * made or bound, surfaces of that kind are plain for the rest of the run;
+ * OMACVM_GL_LOSSLESS=0 keeps them all plain. Shown as a layer's contents they
+ * are checked on macOS 27 only (M1 Max, M2, M4): older systems keep plain
+ * surfaces.
+ */
+static int present_lossless = -1;      /* -1 not read yet, 0 plain, 1 lossless */
+static int present_lossless_half = 1;  /* half-float surfaces too ('&RhA'); 0 after they failed */
 
 /*
  * Colour. The guest renders sRGB unless it says otherwise, so the surfaces
@@ -7825,7 +7846,8 @@ static CGColorSpaceRef cocoa_gl_present_colorspace(bool deep, bool linear)
  */
 static void cocoa_gl_layer_follow(CALayer *layer, IOSurfaceRef surf, bool linear)
 {
-    BOOL hdr = IOSurfaceGetPixelFormat(surf) == 'RGhA' &&
+    OSType fmt = IOSurfaceGetPixelFormat(surf);
+    BOOL hdr = (fmt == 'RGhA' || fmt == '&RhA') &&
                present_color == 1 && (cocoa_gl_present_hdr_wanted() || linear);
     if ([layer wantsExtendedDynamicRangeContent] != hdr) {
         [layer setWantsExtendedDynamicRangeContent:hdr];
@@ -7888,6 +7910,26 @@ static void omacvm_present_gravity(CALayer *layer, IOSurfaceRef surf)
     }
 }
 
+/* A w x h lossless-compressed surface (half: RGBA half float, else BGRA), or NULL. */
+static IOSurfaceRef cocoa_gl_present_packed(uint32_t w, uint32_t h, bool half)
+{
+    CVPixelBufferRef pb = NULL;
+    IOSurfaceRef surf = NULL;
+    NSDictionary *attrs = @{ (id)kCVPixelBufferIOSurfacePropertiesKey: @{} };
+
+    if (CVPixelBufferCreate(kCFAllocatorDefault, w, h,
+                            half ? kCVPixelFormatType_Lossless_64RGBAHalf :
+                                   kCVPixelFormatType_Lossless_32BGRA,
+                            (CFDictionaryRef)attrs, &pb) == kCVReturnSuccess && pb) {
+        surf = CVPixelBufferGetIOSurface(pb);
+        if (surf) {
+            CFRetain(surf);
+        }
+        CVPixelBufferRelease(pb);
+    }
+    return surf;
+}
+
 /*
  * present_ctx is current. Surfaces for a w x h frame, capped at the
  * largest display. Made again at most every PRESENT_REALLOC_NS: until
@@ -7939,6 +7981,28 @@ static bool cocoa_gl_present_alloc(uint32_t w, uint32_t h, bool deep, bool linea
     present_alloc_ns = now;
     present_realloc_due = false;
 
+    if (present_lossless < 0) {
+        const char *e = getenv("OMACVM_GL_LOSSLESS");
+        const char *pd = getenv("OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_DAMAGE");
+        present_lossless = !(e && (!strcmp(e, "0") || !strcmp(e, "off")));
+        if (!present_lossless) {
+            info_report("cocoa: lossless surfaces: off (OMACVM_GL_LOSSLESS)");
+        } else if (pd && !strcmp(pd, "check")) {
+            /*
+             * The partial present's check mode reads the shown surface back
+             * with glReadPixels, which crashes on a compressed one.
+             */
+            present_lossless = 0;
+            info_report("cocoa: lossless surfaces: off (OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_DAMAGE=check reads them back)");
+        } else if (@available(macOS 27.0, *)) {
+            /* checked there */
+        } else {
+            present_lossless = 0;
+            info_report("cocoa: lossless surfaces: off (checked on macOS 27 and newer only)");
+        }
+    }
+again:;
+    bool packed = present_lossless == 1 && (!half || present_lossless_half == 1);
     NSDictionary *props = @{
         (id)kIOSurfaceWidth: @(w),
         (id)kIOSurfaceHeight: @(h),
@@ -7949,7 +8013,8 @@ static bool cocoa_gl_present_alloc(uint32_t w, uint32_t h, bool deep, bool linea
     CFPropertyListRef cs_plist = cs ? CGColorSpaceCopyPropertyList(cs) : NULL;
     bool ok = true;
     for (int i = 0; i < present_nsurf && ok; i++) {
-        present_surf[i] = IOSurfaceCreate((CFDictionaryRef)props);
+        present_surf[i] = packed ? cocoa_gl_present_packed(w, h, half) :
+                                   IOSurfaceCreate((CFDictionaryRef)props);
         if (!present_surf[i]) {
             ok = false;
             break;
@@ -7979,10 +8044,28 @@ static bool cocoa_gl_present_alloc(uint32_t w, uint32_t h, bool deep, bool linea
     }
     CGColorSpaceRelease(cs);
     glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_RECTANGLE, 0);
+    if (!ok && packed) {
+        cocoa_gl_present_free();
+        if (half) {
+            present_lossless_half = 0;
+            warn_report("cocoa: lossless half-float surfaces failed, plain ones from now on");
+        } else {
+            present_lossless = 0;
+            warn_report("cocoa: lossless surfaces failed, plain 8-bit surfaces from now on");
+        }
+        goto again;
+    }
     if (!ok) {
         cocoa_gl_present_free();
         return false;
     }
+    if (!present_packed_logged || packed != present_packed || half != present_packed_half) {
+        present_packed_logged = true;
+        info_report("cocoa: %s surfaces %s", half ? "half-float" : "8-bit",
+                    packed ? "lossless-compressed" : "plain");
+    }
+    present_packed = packed;
+    present_packed_half = half;
     present_w = w;
     present_h = h;
     present_deep = deep;
